      "claim": "The query is alosetron, a 5-HT3 antagonist closely related to ondansetron; ondansetron absolute oral bioavailability is 50-65% after an 8 mg fasted dose (C01), with additional human records of approximately 59%, 50-70%, 60%, and 62 ± 15% (C11, C12, C21, C22).",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C11", "C12", "C21", "C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 ondansetron exposure records show measurable oral Cmax of 33.5 ng/mL (C45) and dose-dependent Cmax ranges of 19.9-348.5 ng/mL across 8-64 mg (C39), consistent with substantial oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C45", "C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 C75 directly reports comparable hepatic clearances of ondansetron, alosetron, and GR87442 in human hepatocytes, supporting transfer of ondansetron's high oral bioavailability to alosetron; C82 reports ondansetron HLM intrinsic clearance of 14.4 µl/min/mg, compatible with the observed 50-65% F, and C84 indicates minimal CYP2D6 contribution. These are mechanistic, not direct F measurements.",
      "card_ids": ["C75", "C82", "C84"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No supplied record provides affirmative evidence of F < 20% for alosetron; the remaining L6 records are either methodological ondansetron hepatocyte comparisons (C76, C81), rat ondansetron metabolite-formation data (C73), or unrelated molecules (C74, C77, C78, C79, C80, C83), and none establishes a low-F liability.",
      "card_ids": ["C73", "C74", "C76", "C77", "C78", "C79", "C80", "C81", "C83"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C73", "C74", "C75", "C76", "C77", "C78", "C79", "C80", "C81", "C82", "C83", "C84"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No alosetron-specific absolute oral bioavailability record; prediction relies on transfer from ondansetron-class analogs and the L6 hepatocyte clearance comparison.",
    "No alosetron-specific oral AUC, Cmax, fed/fasted, formulation, or dose-response data are supplied.",
    "Only C75 directly names alosetron among the L6 hepatic-clearance records, and it is an in vitro hepatocyte clearance comparison rather than an in vivo F measurement.",
    "No alosetron-specific gut-wall efflux, intestinal metabolism, solubility, or dissolution data are supplied."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because alosetron is a close ondansetron-class 5-HT3 antagonist; ondansetron gold records consistently show absolute oral bioavailability around 50-70%, L3 exposure records confirm substantial oral absorption, and L6 C75 shows alosetron hepatic clearance comparable to ondansetron in human hepatocytes, supporting transfer. No affirmative evidence of F < 20% is present."
}

